{
  "schema": "lean-proof-simplification-evidence-v1",
  "source_commit": "6d9e6e43a7707063d9c09935462288e7891ebcc5",
  "scope": "Specialize general least-unit descent for the first represented Pell norm",
  "validation": "Both phases pass the target, ArithmeticPellFirstIndex, ArithmeticPellPowerRecovery and their three focused checks: 12 builds, matching logs without warnings. Enumeration finds the same 32 public/generated declarations, with identical fully elaborated type and axiom reports and the forced discriminant equation theorem. These probes emit eight matching autogenerated-auxiliary warnings in each phase. An independent Lean metaprogram enumerates 17 private declarations and obtains identical type/axiom metadata in both phases. The independent receipt audit and subsequent packaging audit recheck 12 builds, 30 phase-specific local source/object pins, direct project inputs, and 15 graph source snapshots.",
  "limitations": "ArithmeticCarrierSoundness2011 and broader clients were not rebuilt. Foundation, Mathlib and other unaffected dependencies remain authenticated precompiled objects; no full clean build or transitive external dependency audit is claimed. An initial prototype failed because simp made no progress; its log is preserved, but its exact original source snapshot was not retained. A direct private #check/#print attempt failed because Lean rejected private identifiers; the successful private metadata comparison instead uses environment enumeration and collectAxioms, with logs and commands included. Independent private probes did not record elapsed timings. Binary objects and the external Lean toolchain are not included; object hashes and predecessor receipts are included, so this is not a self-contained replay environment.",
  "archive": "inputs-and-logs.zip",
  "archive_sha256": "b817e5a59ef33152b4b19b6f55e0aa0d7147cba2dfa846501f44e03c62190f14",
